#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171856 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172050 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d15f8fa8-f265-50da-b172-3ccb90895448" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Connected Regions"}] :question/id #uuid "8cbffe56-0a93-59c5-9ea8-c4040e07bb03" :question/math-academy-id "e-8682" :question/problem "Which of the following regions are connected?\n\n![](images/ef/ef9e1dfd559c1e8818f14e100e07ab36ca167a4bd2ddf970bf3f5ef325103d64.png)" :question/worked-solution "A region $D$ is connected if every pair of points in $D$ can be joined by a smooth curve or a path in $D.$\n\nAmong the given options, only regions I, II, and III satisfy this definition.\n\nRegion IV does not satisfy this definition. Note that if we take two points $P$ and $Q$, as shown below, there is no path lying entirely within the region that connects them.\n\n![](images/d4/d4d61cf87f2c62c5cf4727384d6dfcc05cada6b23025dd6dd674130eaf64dd45.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171857 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172051 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1af47ea-6253-5d58-9b94-31e52de27106" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Simply-Connected Regions"}] :question/id #uuid "053b6396-341c-5b1f-a942-ca1fbf6efa7a" :question/math-academy-id "e-8684" :question/problem "Which of the regions shown below are simply connected?\n\n![](images/b8/b8e630b749cbfee41d73a620ffd284f3216bb8a43affdc26543f1eb57e4613c5.png)" :question/worked-solution "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](images/7d/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](images/c3/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the regions: \n\n- Region I is not simply connected. Instead, this is a connected region that contains a hole.\n\n- Region II is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n\n- Region III is not simply connected. Instead, this is a region that consists of two pieces (it's not connected).\n\n- Region IV is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171897 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172091 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "280e7ba4-7617-546b-9e0d-a5bdc33dad8d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Simply-Connected Regions in Euclidian Space"}] :question/id #uuid "fb87998f-3236-510b-94aa-7db80487d8c9" :question/math-academy-id "e-9498" :question/problem "Which of the following regions are simply connected?\n\n- $\\{(x,y) \\in \\mathbb R^2 \\: | \\: y-x\\geq 0\\}$\n\n- $\\{(x,y) \\in \\mathbb R^2 \\: | \\: (x,y)\\neq (0,0)\\}$\n\n- $\\{(x,y)\\in \\mathbb R^2 \\: | \\: x^2+y^2> 4\\}$" :question/worked-solution "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](images/7d/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](images/c3/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nLet's now examine our regions in turn.\n\n- Region I is simply connected. Indeed, it is the half-plane $y \\geq x.$ So, it's a plane region without holes.\n\n- Region II is *not*  simply connected since it's a plane region with a hole at $(0,0).$\n\n- Region III is *not* simply connected since it's a plane region with a hole. In this case, the hole contains all points on the disc $x^2+y^2 \\leq 4$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259573 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172050 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d15f8fa8-f265-50da-b172-3ccb90895448" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Connected Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fd295e1-1f3f-51b0-a531-01895286cbb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ae/ae77eaad51b8cd6bff4e62032946254da948e7643b45bd5e3a2343462ac457cb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257203} {:answer/id #uuid "7d496aba-750d-5723-bcf6-4b18fd5ca5ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/10/1067a6abc2249b31f3786a3f277a2db10d8f32cbacf971a550a0473243684da7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257888} {:answer/id #uuid "a6346f12-fe1a-52b3-ae64-8730d965aa8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/98/98a0e2e2cd960a8065d83ce53336a727709d0228d43e28d3aed216f755aaafaa.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258231} {:answer/id #uuid "b4d4af53-2db6-53e6-a9dc-bf20307ab33f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6c/6c5f1576f6882e6e72633e7eb707f77d2707e0afa76307403848a58a8f45689a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258349} {:answer/id #uuid "b9912de7-1c35-55de-a866-f90635b99433" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/27/2725284d21ba0b2514e5043ce1f776338e0480e0bb50c26234fae0a7d12d404c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258406}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d496aba-750d-5723-bcf6-4b18fd5ca5ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/10/1067a6abc2249b31f3786a3f277a2db10d8f32cbacf971a550a0473243684da7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257888} :answer-field/id #uuid "8cb37ec1-d922-5b73-967a-f71d5b47a3a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259273}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "856afbeb-9f59-56e5-affb-452bd8050ce2" :question/math-academy-id "q-123882" :question/problem "Which of the following regions is *not* connected?" :question/worked-solution "A region $D$ is connected if every pair of points in $D$ can be joined by a smooth curve or a path in $D.$ \n\nAmong the given options, the only one that does not satisfy this definition is the following:\n\n![](images/10/1067a6abc2249b31f3786a3f277a2db10d8f32cbacf971a550a0473243684da7.png)\n\n \n\nNote that if we take two points $P$ and $Q$, as shown below, there is no path lying entirely within the region that connects them.\n\n![](images/2b/2bcaaf15d709d6396155bcdc9e8976bb037c9f341fc0b8863687958dbb0f40ff.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259574 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172051 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1af47ea-6253-5d58-9b94-31e52de27106" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Simply-Connected Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a04266f-fa97-5bc9-a110-7f2c8e8f9f80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ba/ba9b18a202db25c02b0907665d24fca75c9f4afc5babe898ff8f9c0227c7d447.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257297} {:answer/id #uuid "57b08ac5-e8a1-54f3-9c10-b1e40e64ae98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/82/82a33d59ae0060b0f1187415698ccf36ae45bd4ddc1fce0af74d01df74356ee1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257541} {:answer/id #uuid "88567626-0735-5cdd-944f-a824128be66a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/imag